## Decisions the plan didn't spell out

- **Expiry boundary**: an entry is considered expired when `now() >= setTime + ttlMs`, so at exactly `ttlMs` after setting it is gone (a `get` at that instant returns `undefined`).
- **Eviction happens from the recency front only** (lazy deletion). Expired entries are dropped when they are accessed, swept by `size`, or reach the front during eviction; they never make the physical map exceed `capacity`. I chose this over eagerly purging expired entries mid-map because it keeps every operation amortized O(1) under plain LRU churn, which matches the literal "least recently used entry is evicted first" wording.
- **`delete` of an expired entry returns `false`**, since "expired entries counting as absent" makes them behave like a key the `Map` never had.
- `set`/`get` refresh recency only; expiry time is refreshed by `set` alone, never by `get` (per "expiring ttlMs after it was set").

